{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/774641-apocalypse-tribe-s-one-song","id":774641,"title":"Apocalypse: Tribe's One Song...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-26T03:14:21-08:00","id":774641,"title":"Apocalypse: Tribe's One Song...","content":"...for the Weaver.<br /> <br /> So I asked before, earlier in the Werewolf: The Apocalypse thread what tribe would you have fall to the Wyrm and how, during the Apocalypse? Had some really great answers. <br /> <br /> Here I ask, rather than fall to the Wyrm, what Tribe would you have fall to the Weaver instead? <br /> <br /> In one game scenario I made the prophecies and dark forboding omens suggest Two Tribes would fall. To my joy, everyone assumed that meant to the Wyrm. So they over looked the glasswalkers who were making great progress and strides in their fields and showed no signs of wyrm like behaviour in their investigations.<br /> <br /> now I look back and I'm like, 'I took the easy and obvious route on that choice. I should have had it be another tribe' not that there's anything wrong in sometimes taking tbe easy and obvious route. Just that I think I should have tried more to make the Weaver gaining a hold on a whole tribe much deeper and richer from a shock and horror perspective. <br /> <br /> I'm running a game currently with dark portents leading upto the apocalypse and this time I'm planting seeds in each tribe to be the potential Weaver and Wyrm tribe.<br /> <br /> my current favourite for the Weaver is the Black Furies. The Wyld warriors look on and try to hold back the despair as they watch the Weaver ascend over the Wyld. The Wyrm rising in tornent as continues to feed of everything and twist all things in its coils. Then they see the weaver hold a victory over wyrm and they wonder..if the weaver could defeat the wyrm...could they turn the weavers own weapons against it to free or empower the wyld. <br /> <br /> All good intentions. Arguments and questions have begun with regards to the wyld and weaver connections. Rain can fall randomly anywhere, but it always falls down. What would the tribe have been like had the Weaver not shown them the bow? Arent tapestries of life and our stories woven upon the loom Etc etc<br /> <br /> sure enough it begins with the best intentions. Fight with the Weaver against the Wyrm to give the Wyld a chance to recover. Then turn the shared weaver weapons, knowledges and abilities against it to empower the wyld further. <br /> <br /> If you picked a tribe to go Team Weaver, which tribe would it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T14:40:36-08:00","id":775037,"title":"","content":"I couldn't answer in the Wyrm one because of potential spoilers in case a player happened into the topic, but for this one: the Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> I feel like they are a candidate even moreso than the Glass Walkers, because they represent the core values of the Weaver, whereas the Glass Walkers have been more taking advantage of it but remaining malleable and flexible. Silver Fangs strive for control and perfection, using tradition as their guidebook. When they cannot have their very particular way about things, they lapse into psychosis, and terrible things tend to result. <i>Sounds awfully familiar...</i><br /> <br /> In my games, I tend to track Triatic alignment of most things, and the Silver Fangs as a tribe have a great deal of Static/Weaver in their court. While the Nation at large is wary of the urrah for their proximity to the Weaver, the Silver Fangs have been losing their shit with their inability to maintain control of the Nation, and their desire for order (under their command) and harmony (under their command) and their already prevalent madness makes them ideal listeners to the Weaver's whispers. After all, the Weaver had been there, know what its like, and wants largely the same things (albeit on a much more cosmic scale).<br /> <br /> The other tribe I like playing around with Weaver-fallen notions is the Red Talons, for somewhat similar reasons of tradition and trying desperately to hold on to a status quo that no longer exists. Like the Silver Fangs, there is a great deal of rigidity in their tribe, dogged adherence to certain values that reinforce a very specific role in the world, a place in the hierarchy and ecosystem, and a refusal of things outside of that paradigm. They love the Wyld, they fight for Gaia, but their ideals doesn't fully match up with their actions, especially on a historical scale. That said, I don't think the Red Talons would be nearly as useful to the Weaver as the Silver Fang, and a fall to the webs would go largely, tragically unnoticed as they continue to slip to extinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T14:50:49-08:00","id":775047,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the mad silver fangs joining with insane weaver to gain more control over the universe as a whole. With goals to break apart the lodges and make luna and helios bless them equally and other such lofty goals where the rest of the world is now only worth a boot heel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah I like the Red Talons for a weaver fall too. But I wouldnt wanter to tech them out or fill them with cybertech. I think maybe have it channel through them on a primal level. Their senses and insight comes in with weaver like efficiency and clarity. Their understabding and nature of things expands. They command the weavers spirits and forces on a primal level of Rageful dominance or pack mentality and are the alpha apex of the weaver. Everything benefits or everything is prey in the name of the weaver. the one who stopped them from becoming extinct and in the future put humans in zoos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}